 "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rgZW4VRRGTo",
 "title": "Handle Any Cold Call Objection",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains a framework to handle cold call objections using APA: Acknowledge, Permission, and Ask Questions. This approach helps lower the prospect's guard and creates an opening to continue the conversation.",
 "key_points": [
  "Use the APA framework: Acknowledge, Permission, and Ask Questions.",
  "Acknowledge the objection to lower the prospect's guard.",
  "Ask for permission before asking a follow-up question.",
  "For 'I'm not interested', respond: 'Completely understand, letting you go. Before I let you go, can I ask you a question? Is this because you don't want the service or because it's a random cold call?'",
  "For 'Send me an email', respond: '100%, sending you an email right away. Can I ask you a question? What would you like to see in that email?'"
 ],
 "content": "The creator shares a method to handle objections on cold calls called APA, which stands for Acknowledge, Permission, and Ask questions. The creator claims that acknowledging lowers the prospect's guard, taking permission respects their time, and asking questions gives you an opening that can enter you into a meeting. Scenario one: Somebody says, 'I'm not interested!' Response: \"Completely understand, letting you go. Before I let you go, can I ask you a question? Is this because you don't want the service or because it's a random cold call?\" Scenario two: Somebody says, 'Send me an email'. Response: \"100%, sending you an email right away. Can I ask you a question? What would you like to see in that email?\"",
 "status": "done",
